OSKit Arch -- x86_64 PCI config-space + enumeration
=====================================================

Port-based PCI configuration access (0xCF8/0xCFC), device
enumeration, BAR decoding, and capability-list walk. This is the
x86-specific transport plumbing that sits underneath
`virtio_transport_pci.lsysl` — this file knows nothing about
virtio except for the vendor ID + modern-device ID range used by
`pci_find_virtio`.

QEMU's `pc` / `q35` machines expose a flat bus 0 and we don't
walk behind PCI-to-PCI bridges; for virtio-net in QEMU that's
not a concern. Multi-bus walking is a future problem.

    module oskit.arch.x86_64


32-bit port I/O (implemented in boot.s as proper `outl`/`inl`
instructions). The byte-wide `outb`/`inb` the rest of the
runtime uses aren't sufficient for PCI — the host bridge expects
a single 4-byte bus cycle per config access.

    extern outl(port: int, v: u32)
    extern inl(port: int) -> u32


Config-space port addresses.

    val PCI_CONFIG_ADDRESS = 0xCF8
    val PCI_CONFIG_DATA    = 0xCFC


Standard type-0 header offsets we actually touch.

    val PCI_CFG_VENDOR        = 0x00
    val PCI_CFG_DEVICE        = 0x02
    val PCI_CFG_COMMAND       = 0x04
    val PCI_CFG_STATUS_REG    = 0x06
    val PCI_CFG_BAR0          = 0x10
    val PCI_CFG_CAP_PTR       = 0x34


Command-register bits we set.

    val PCI_CMD_MEM_SPACE     = 0x0002
    val PCI_CMD_BUS_MASTER    = 0x0004

Status-register bit 4 — "has capability list at offset 0x34".

    val PCI_STATUS_CAP_LIST   = 0x0010


Generic PCI capability ID. 0x09 is vendor-specific — virtio uses
this for every one of its COMMON/NOTIFY/ISR/DEVICE caps.

    val PCI_CAP_VENDOR        = 0x09


BAR decoding. Memory BARs have bit 0 = 0; bits 1-2 encode the
locator (00 = 32-bit, 10 = 64-bit); bit 3 = prefetchable. The
usable base is `bar & ~0xf`. I/O BARs (bit 0 = 1) are ignored
— virtio-pci modern places everything in memory BARs.

    val PCI_BAR_IO_MASK             = 0x1
    val PCI_BAR_TYPE_64             = 0x4
    val PCI_BAR_ADDR_MASK_MEM: u32  = 0xFFFFFFF0


Virtio-over-PCI constants. Modern virtio devices present vendor
0x1AF4 and device ID 0x1040 + `virtio_device_id` (so 0x1041 for
net, 0x1042 for block, …). The transitional range
(0x1000..0x103F) isn't supported; the driver requires VERSION_1
which only modern devices offer.

    val VIRTIO_PCI_VENDOR: int       = 0x1AF4
    val VIRTIO_PCI_MODERN_BASE: int  = 0x1040

Virtio capability `cfg_type` values (the byte at offset 3 of a
vendor-specific virtio cap).

    val VIRTIO_PCI_CAP_COMMON_CFG    = 1
    val VIRTIO_PCI_CAP_NOTIFY_CFG    = 2
    val VIRTIO_PCI_CAP_ISR_CFG       = 3
    val VIRTIO_PCI_CAP_DEVICE_CFG    = 4
    val VIRTIO_PCI_CAP_PCI_CFG       = 5

Virtio cap byte layout (all offsets from the cap header start):

- 0: cap_vndr   (= 0x09)
- 1: cap_next
- 2: cap_len
- 3: cfg_type
- 4: bar
- 5: id
- 6..7: padding
- 8..11: offset (u32, little-endian)
- 12..15: length (u32, little-endian)
- 16..19: notify_off_multiplier (u32, only if cfg_type == NOTIFY_CFG)

    val VPCI_CAP_CFG_TYPE        = 3
    val VPCI_CAP_BAR             = 4
    val VPCI_CAP_OFFSET          = 8
    val VPCI_CAP_LENGTH          = 12
    val VPCI_CAP_NOTIFY_MULT     = 16


BDF packing. High byte: bus, next 5 bits: device, low 3 bits:
function. -1 means "no device".

    val PCI_BDF_NONE = -1

    pci_bdf(bus: int, dev: int, fn: int) -> int
        (bus << 8) | (dev << 3) | (fn & 0x7)

    pci_bdf_bus(bdf: int) -> int
        (bdf >> 8) & 0xff

    pci_bdf_dev(bdf: int) -> int
        (bdf >> 3) & 0x1f

    pci_bdf_fn(bdf: int) -> int
        bdf & 0x7


Pack (bus, dev, fn, off) into the 32-bit value 0xCF8 expects.
`off` must be 4-byte aligned; the byte/word readers fold in the
low bits on the data-port side.

    pci_cfg_addr(bus: int, dev: int, fn: int, off: int) -> u32
        val b = u32(bus & 0xff) << 16
        val d = u32(dev & 0x1f) << 11
        val f = u32(fn  & 0x07) << 8
        val o = u32(off & 0xfc)
        u32(0x80000000) | b | d | f | o


32-bit config-space read/write.

    pci_read32(bdf: int, off: int) -> u32
        outl(PCI_CONFIG_ADDRESS,
             pci_cfg_addr(pci_bdf_bus(bdf), pci_bdf_dev(bdf),
                          pci_bdf_fn(bdf), off))
        inl(PCI_CONFIG_DATA)

    pci_write32(bdf: int, off: int, v: u32)
        outl(PCI_CONFIG_ADDRESS,
             pci_cfg_addr(pci_bdf_bus(bdf), pci_bdf_dev(bdf),
                          pci_bdf_fn(bdf), off))
        outl(PCI_CONFIG_DATA, v)


16- and 8-bit readers — align down, shift.

    pci_read16(bdf: int, off: int) -> int
        val dword = pci_read32(bdf, off & ~3)
        val shift = (off & 2) * 8
        int((dword >> u32(shift)) & u32(0xffff))

    pci_read8(bdf: int, off: int) -> int
        val dword = pci_read32(bdf, off & ~3)
        val shift = (off & 3) * 8
        int((dword >> u32(shift)) & u32(0xff))

Read/modify/write for 16-bit fields, preserving dword neighbours.

    pci_write16(bdf: int, off: int, v: int)
        val dword = pci_read32(bdf, off & ~3)
        val shift = (off & 2) * 8
        val mask  = u32(0xffff) << u32(shift)
        val updated = (dword & ~mask) | ((u32(v & 0xffff)) << u32(shift))
        pci_write32(bdf, off & ~3, updated)


Vendor + device IDs. Vendor 0xFFFF indicates "no device here" —
PCI returns all-ones for an absent slot.

    pci_vendor(bdf: int) -> int
        pci_read16(bdf, PCI_CFG_VENDOR)

    pci_device(bdf: int) -> int
        pci_read16(bdf, PCI_CFG_DEVICE)


Walk bus 0, function 0 of each slot, for the first virtio
device of `dev_id`. Returns the matching BDF or `PCI_BDF_NONE`.
We don't probe function > 0: virtio isn't multi-function in
QEMU, and skipping the multi-function bit keeps the walk tiny.

    pci_find_virtio(dev_id: int) -> int
        val target = VIRTIO_PCI_MODERN_BASE + dev_id
        var d = 0
        while d < 32
            val bdf = pci_bdf(0, d, 0)
            if pci_vendor(bdf) == VIRTIO_PCI_VENDOR
                if pci_device(bdf) == target
                    return bdf
            d += 1
        PCI_BDF_NONE


Enable memory decoding + bus mastering. Required before the CPU
can touch any MMIO BAR and before the device can DMA.

    pci_enable(bdf: int)
        val cmd = pci_read16(bdf, PCI_CFG_COMMAND)
        pci_write16(bdf, PCI_CFG_COMMAND,
            cmd | PCI_CMD_MEM_SPACE | PCI_CMD_BUS_MASTER)


BAR decoding. Reads BAR[i] (0..5). For a 32-bit memory BAR,
returns the base address. For a 64-bit memory BAR (type bits =
0b10), stitches BAR[i] and BAR[i+1] into a 64-bit address.
Returns 0 for I/O BARs (we don't consume them) or unused BARs
(which read as 0).

    pci_bar_raw(bdf: int, i: int) -> u32
        pci_read32(bdf, PCI_CFG_BAR0 + i * 4)

    pci_bar_is_64(bdf: int, i: int) -> int
        val raw = pci_bar_raw(bdf, i)
        if (raw & u32(PCI_BAR_IO_MASK)) != 0
            return 0
        if (raw & u32(PCI_BAR_TYPE_64)) != 0
            return 1
        0

    pci_bar_addr(bdf: int, i: int) -> u64
        val raw = pci_bar_raw(bdf, i)
        if (raw & u32(PCI_BAR_IO_MASK)) != 0
            return u64(0)
        val low = u64(raw & PCI_BAR_ADDR_MASK_MEM)
        if (raw & u32(PCI_BAR_TYPE_64)) != 0
            val hi = u64(pci_bar_raw(bdf, i + 1))
            return (hi << 32) | low
        low


Find the first virtio vendor-specific capability whose
`cfg_type` matches. The caller usually wants the four
well-known types (COMMON / NOTIFY / ISR / DEVICE); duplicates
are rare enough that "find the first" is the right default.

Returns the config-space offset of the cap header, or -1 if
not present.

    pci_find_virtio_cap(bdf: int, cfg_type: int) -> int
        val status = pci_read16(bdf, PCI_CFG_STATUS_REG)
        if (status & PCI_STATUS_CAP_LIST) == 0
            return -1
        var off = pci_read8(bdf, PCI_CFG_CAP_PTR) & 0xfc
        var guard = 48
        while off != 0 && guard > 0
            val id = pci_read8(bdf, off)
            if id == PCI_CAP_VENDOR
                val t = pci_read8(bdf, off + VPCI_CAP_CFG_TYPE)
                if t == cfg_type
                    return off
            off = pci_read8(bdf, off + 1) & 0xfc
            guard -= 1
        -1


Read a u32 virtio-cap field (offset, length, notify_off_
multiplier). Virtio caps store little-endian u32 at byte
granularity in config space; the containing dwords aren't
aligned the same way the cap header is, so assemble from 4
byte reads.

    pci_cap_u32(bdf: int, cap_off: int, field_off: int) -> u32
        val b0 = u32(pci_read8(bdf, cap_off + field_off)     & 0xff)
        val b1 = u32(pci_read8(bdf, cap_off + field_off + 1) & 0xff)
        val b2 = u32(pci_read8(bdf, cap_off + field_off + 2) & 0xff)
        val b3 = u32(pci_read8(bdf, cap_off + field_off + 3) & 0xff)
        b0 | (b1 << 8) | (b2 << 16) | (b3 << 24)
